 of pemphigus in south-western Iran: a 10-year retrospective study (1991-2000). <source>Int J Dermatol</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>45</volume>:<fpage>103</fpage>-5.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16445496</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="other">Gellis S, Glass FA. Pemphigus: a survey of one hundred and seventy patients admitted to Bellevue Hospital from 1911 to 1941. <source>Arch Dermatol Syphiol</source><year>1941</year>;44.</citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Uzun S, Durdu M, Akman A, Gunasti S, Uslular C, Memisoglu HR, et al. Pemphigus in the Mediterranean region of Turkey: a study of 148 cases. <source>Int J Dermatol</source><year>2006</year>;<volume>45</volume>:<fpage>523</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16700784</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Ryan JG. Pemphigus: a 20-year survey of experience with 70 cases. <source>Arch Dermatol</source><year>1971</year>;<volume>104</volume>:<fpage>14</fpage>-20.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4330419</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Lewis JD, Schinnar R, Bilker WB, Wang X, Strom BL. Validation studies of the health improvement network (THIN) database for pharmacoepidemiology research. <source>Pharmacoepidemiol Drug Saf</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>16</volume>:<fpage>393</fpage>-401.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17066486</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal">Bath-Hextall F, Leonardi-Bee J, Smith C, Meal A, Hubbard R. Trends in incidence of skin basal cell carcinoma: additional evidence from a UK primary care database study. <source>Int J Cancer</source><year>2007</year>;<volume>121</volume>:<fpage>2105</fpage>-8.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17640064</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal">Lewis JD, Schinnar R,